2200 GOSUB 6380:BM$="Owner: Oh my, if it isn't David! I see Alan, Andrew, and Martin are with you.\You've just come back today, haven't you?":GOSUB 5100
2210 BM$="Owner: It's so good to see you! It's pretty much impossible for Eleno Vision\to play here now, but that just means you've made it big.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
2220 GOSUB 6305:BM$="David: We wanted you to be the first to hear about our success. We owe you\a lot. We probably wouldn't be where we are if not for you.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
2230 GOSUB 6380:BM$="Owner: I'm glad to hear that. How about we move to the counter? It's still\small and cramped as usual, but we can push some customers away.":GOSUB 5100
2235 GOSUB 6170:W8=0:GOSUB 6380:BM$="The owner asked some customers to move away, and lined up some chairs\from the dressing room at the counter.":GOSUB 5100
2236 BM$="Owner: Boy, serve us some scotch... No, not that one! Our finest scotch! It's\my treat, friends. Bottoms up!":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
2240 GOSUB 6310:BM$="Martin: It's been a while since we've been here! Jimmy's performing\tonight, huh? Guess he's your main performer now.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
2250 GOSUB 6320:BM$="Alan: I remember when we used to be the main performers here. The pay\was so low we'd spend most of it on the ride back home.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
2260 GOSUB 6380:BM$="Owner: Hey, amateurs should be grateful to even get a chance to play. And\small as it is, getting a pay makes you feel like a professional. Honestly, I'm\a beacon of hope for all you whippersnappers.":GOSUB 5100
2261 BM$="Before long, the customers around the counter were staring at David.":GOSUB 5100
2262 GOSUB 6195:BM$="Jimmy, on stage, knew that Eleno Vision was in the club, and that made him\anxious. Once his performance was over, he took the microphone.":GOSUB 5100
2263 BM$="Jimmy: Ladies and gentlemen, we have some special guests! Eleno Vision is\here!":GOSUB 5100
2264 BM$="The customers started murmuring, looking around for David and the band.":GOSUB 5100
2265 BM$="Jimmy: How about you sing for us, David? It might be the last time Eleno\Vision performs here!":GOSUB 5100
2266 BM$="Jimmy: Please! They all want to hear you sing!":GOSUB 5100
2267 GOSUB 9515:W8=0:BM$="The guests started clapping, clamoring for Eleno Vision to get on the\stage.":GOSUB 5100
2268 GOSUB 6170:GOSUB 6380:GOSUB 9505
2270 BM$="Owner: Jimmy, for Pete's sake... I'm sorry it came to this. Could I ask you to\sing? Just one song, to please the crowd.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
2280 GOSUB 6330:BM$="Andrew: Well, you heard him. Are you up for it?":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
2290 GOSUB 6320:BM$="Alan: I say we owe him this much. Let's do it, David. It'll be like that time in\Italy.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
2300 GOSUB 6300:BM$="David: I'm pretty tired... I hope I have the energy for it. Never thought our\first live in London would be at Marquee!":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
2310 GOSUB 6310:BM$="Martin: We're lucky David's tired. At his best he'd bring down the whole\building!":GOSUB 5100
2320 BM$="The band went up on the stage.":GOSUB 5100
2330 GOSUB 6150:BM$="The clapping turned to cheers. That night, the lights of the Marquee Club\stayed lit until morning.":GOSUB 5100
